  "review": "Independently reviewed all 78 exact test call paths after integrating main accf6fc7. Prompt deserialization, block construction, level/request validation, argv and YAML rendering are pure. Manager tests use SessionState, Noop emitter and in-memory channels for accepted/rejected/cancelled/cleared/switched model and provider snapshots; Office has no mentioned scene and memory has no installed database handle, so both return before external access. SDK-effort tests use only private temporary JSON and a non-executed placeholder; cache fingerprint/get/put read filesystem metadata/configuration and access an in-memory map. Claude, Codex, Pi and DSH lifecycle fixtures use fake JSONL peers or temporary Python processes, SessionState, Noop emitters and private transcript files, never real runtimes. The two merged Pi regressions cover resumed route/default-effort changes with same-turn steering and legacy print effort/route arguments. The merged DSH regression records set/clear/omitted effort YAML across three turns while preserving steering. Their cfg(test) seed helper only fingerprints the isolated launch context and populates the metadata cache; PI_CODING_AGENT_DIR/DSH_HOME and the executable/working directory are private temporary paths. Driver resolve_turn reaches inspect only through its cache-hit return and never reaches native run_probe, SDK imports or real model requests. DSH generated codeg-*.patch.yml is excluded from the configuration fingerprint, keeping the seeded cache valid after patch publication. Shared ledger/readiness tests use only in-memory state/channels. Native ACP tests use JSON, SessionState, Notify/Mutex and in-memory duplex reactors; receipt history uses the temporary transcript writer with CODEG_HOME scoped to a private temporary directory. Owned-bootstrap tests use pure environment planning, private temporary files and worker threads, never AppState or a database. Separately reviewed effort Node tests call pure wire checks, mock metadata/selection, read-only temporary settings, per-model default getters and sampling merges with CODEG_PI_EFFORT_PROBE=0; runner apply and SDK probe entry points are excluded. Owned runtime Node/Python tests use fixed source fragments, fake Agents/processes and pure ACP SDK routing, never the full application or SQLite. Recursive resource fingerprinting includes production mjs/cjs/js/py/json, including the three main effort resources, exactly once. ReceiptBatch closes history before successor admission; late acknowledgements remain unconfirmed. No allowlisted call chain creates AppDatabase, SQLite, migrations, seeds, network connections or a real Agent/provider. Real-instance observations and all unlisted suites remain excluded from execution. Regenerate the source fingerprint only after the merged production/test call chains are reviewed and frozen. The runner-only YAML regression constructs an in-memory DshLaunchProfile, calls render_patch_with_options and parses the returned string with serde_yaml; it checks a single two-row runner sequence and a valid zero-row stock sequence. It performs no file I/O or process/runtime/database initialization. The reviewed production fix omits an empty serialized prefix only when a runner sequence follows; ordinary empty stock patches remain [].",
